cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fedcausal: federated causal structure learning for Bayesian networks"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Torrijos Arenas"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Castilla-La Mancha"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ptorrijos99/fedcausal"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  fedcausal learns the structure of a discrete Bayesian network across several
  sites without moving data between them. Each site runs greedy equivalence
  search locally, a coordinator combines the resulting graphs by structural
  consensus fusion, and only graphs and scores cross the network. It runs
  in-process for experiments and over Flower for deployment.
keywords:
  - causal discovery
  - structure learning
  - Bayesian networks
  - federated learning
  - greedy equivalence search
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Optimal structure identification with greedy search"
    authors:
      - family-names: Chickering
        given-names: "David Maxwell"
    journal: "Journal of Machine Learning Research"
    volume: 3
    year: 2002
    start: 507
    end: 554
  - type: article
    title: "Efficient and accurate structural fusion of Bayesian networks"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Puerta"
